## What Wireshark Is
A tool that captures and shows raw network traffic in real time, packet by packet.

## Interface Layout
- **Packet list** (top) — one line per packet
- **Packet details** (middle) — protocol layers (Ethernet → IP → TCP/UDP → app layer)
- **Packet bytes** (bottom) — raw hex/ASCII

## Capturing Traffic
- Pick a network interface, start the capture, stop when done
- **Capture filter** = limits what gets recorded (set before starting)
- **Display filter** = hides/shows already-captured packets (used anytime)

## Useful Display Filters
```
ip.addr == 10.49.167.162
tcp.port == 443
http

```

## Color Coding
Wireshark colors packets by type so you can scan quickly:
- Green → HTTP
- Light blue → TCP
- Black → errors

## Following a Conversation
Right-click a packet → Follow → TCP Stream, to see the full exchange between client and server.

## Saving Work
Captures can be saved as `.pcap` / `.pcapng` files for later analysis.

